---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Plain-language terms of use. Kept short and consistent with EDITORIAL.md:
// the record links to its sources, other outlets and creators are attributed,
// and corrections are visible. The effective date is the date of the last
// substantive edit.
const MAIL = "corrections@chinovalley.today";
const EFFECTIVE = "November 10, 2026";
---

<Base
	title="Terms of use — Chino Valley Today"
	description="The terms for using Chino Valley Today: what the site is, what it promises, and what it does not."
>
	<header class="legalhead">
		<div class="shell legalhead__inner">
			<h1 class="legalhead__title">Terms of use</h1>
			<p class="legalhead__date mark">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<div class="reading body prose">
		<p>
			These terms apply to chinovalley.today and its feeds. By using the site
			you agree to them. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains
			what the site collects. If anything here is unclear, email
			<a href={`mailto:${MAIL}`}>{MAIL}</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>What the site is</h2>
		<p>
			Chino Valley Today is an independent local news site covering Chino and
			Chino Hills. Most of it is assembled from public records by software,
			some of it written by AI language models, and most entries publish
			without a person reading them first. AI-written entries pass automated
			checks first, and a person reviews the most sensitive items, as
			described on the
			<a href="/about/">About</a> page. It is not affiliated with the City of
			Chino, the City of Chino Hills, the Chino Valley Unified School District,
			or any agency it covers.
		</p>

		<h2>The record is the authority</h2>
		<p>
			Reports here about what a public body did link to the record they came
			from. We work to get each one right and we correct mistakes visibly, but
			the site is provided as is, without warranties of any kind, express or
			implied, including that it is accurate or complete. If this site and the
			official record disagree, go by the record. Nothing here is legal or
			other professional advice. Do not rely on the site alone for legal,
			financial, safety, or deadline-sensitive decisions; follow the link and
			confirm with the agency. During an emergency, follow official alerts and
			instructions.
		</p>

		<h2>Other people's content</h2>
		<p>
			Headlines and short excerpts from other news outlets are attributed to
			them and link to their articles, which belong to their publishers.
			Videos from local creators play from TikTok, which hosts them, and
			belong to their creators. We feature a post or a story to point readers
			to it. Featuring it does not endorse it, and what a creator or another
			outlet says is their statement, not ours.
		</p>
		<p>
			A featured creator who wants a video or their profile removed can email
			<a href={`mailto:${MAIL}`}>{MAIL}</a>, and we will remove it promptly. A
			publisher with a concern about how its work appears here can email the
			same address.
		</p>

		<h2>Using what is here</h2>
		<p>
			You are welcome to read, link to, quote, and share the site's own
			writing, with credit to Chino Valley Today and a link back. Public
			records and archived agency documents remain public records, and we
			claim no ownership of them. Please do not republish the site in bulk or
			present it as your own.
		</p>
		<p>
			Automated access is welcome within reason: use the
			<a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> where you can, identify your tool
			honestly, and keep request rates modest. Do not attempt to disrupt the
			site or get around its security.
		</p>

		<h2>Corrections</h2>
		<p>
			If something here is wrong, tell us. Corrections are normally made
			openly: the original text stays, struck through, with a dated note. We
			may remove text entirely, with a note saying so, where leaving it
			visible would cause harm, such as a name that should not have been
			published. See
			<a href="/about/">About</a> for how corrections are handled.
		</p>

		<h2>Liability</h2>
		<p>
			To the extent the law allows, Chino Valley Today and the people who run
			it are not liable for any loss or damage, direct or indirect, arising
			from errors or omissions on the site, your use of it or reliance on it,
			or the sites and services it links to.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes and governing law</h2>
		<p>
			These terms may change, and the effective date at the top will change
			with them. Using the site after a change means you accept the updated
			terms. These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.legalhead {
		background: var(--crate);
		color: #fff;
		border-bottom: 6px solid var(--placard);
	}
	.legalhead__inner {
		padding-block: 1.9rem 2.2rem;
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	.legalhead__title {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 1.2rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
		line-height: 1.16;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.legalhead__date {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
	}
	.body {
		padding-block: 2.4rem 1rem;
	}
</style>
